# The app's own startup path.
#
# Android's profile installer reads this from the app and asks the compiler to prepare these
# classes ahead of time, so the first frame does not wait for the compiler to catch up.
#
# The wildcard covers the whole app. The app is small — under a megabyte of its own code — so
# preparing all of it costs a moment at install time and saves the wait every time the app is
# opened. The libraries bring their own profiles, which AGP merges with this one.
HSPLapp/daylog/**;->**(**)**
